    "knowledge_point": "Solving a 2x2 System of Equations Using an Inverse Matrix With Reorganization",
    "problem": "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=4 \\\\ x=-2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y=4 \\\\ x+2y=-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
